{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>וְהָיָה כִי יְבִיאֲךָ ה' אֶל אֶרֶץ הַכְּנַעֲנִי</b> Although He enumerated only five nations, all seven nations are implied, for they are all included under Canaanite, and one of the families was called by no other name but Canaanite. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 13:5). And in truth they are included under Canaanite because they are all his sons (Genesis 10:15–16), and therefore when He says (Exodus 13:11) \"וְהָיָה כִּי יְבִיאֲךָ ה' אֶל אֶרֶץ הַכְּנַעֲנִי,\" it includes all of them, and so too Scripture says in every place \"אֶרֶץ כְּנַעַן.\" But here there is no reason for Him to mention most of them and leave some included under Canaanite.<br>And the opinion of our Sages (Sifrei Deuteronomy 26:9) is that the land of these five nations was a land flowing with milk and honey, and the land of the two remaining ones was not so, and therefore He proclaims to them about this land. Thus we learned in the Sifrei regarding the matter of first fruits: \"וַיִּתֶּן לָנוּ אֶת הָאָרֶץ הַזֹּאת אֶרֶץ זָבַת חָלָב וּדְבַשׁ\" — just as \"a land flowing with milk and honey\" stated there refers to the land of the five nations, so too \"a land flowing with milk and honey\" stated here refers to the land of seven nations. Rabbi Yosi says: one does not bring first fruits from beyond the Jordan, for it is not flowing with milk and honey. You see that they excluded the land of the two nations from first fruits because it is not flowing with milk and honey, and Rabbi Yosi excluded even Transjordan, which belonged to the Amorite, because it too is not flowing with milk and honey; and the Amorite mentioned here is the one in the land of Israel itself. And to this effect it is taught in the Mekhilta in this pericope. And it is further taught in the Sifrei (Deuteronomy 18:2): \"וְנַחֲלָה לֹא יִהְיֶה לוֹ\" — this is the inheritance of the five nations; \"בְּקֶרֶב אֶחָיו\" — this is the inheritance of the two nations. They set these five nations apart by themselves because they are the core of the land concerning which He promised them that it is flowing with milk and honey. And Rashi in the pericope of Judges and Officers (ibid.) raised a difficulty with this baraita. And according to this opinion, the verse above (3:8) \"אֶל אֶרֶץ טוֹבָה וּרְחָבָה אֶל אֶרֶץ זָבַת חָלָב וּדְבַשׁ\" — it was not on account of \"flowing with milk and honey\" that He added the Perizzite there, but rather on account of \"a good and spacious land,\" and they are the six nations mentioned everywhere, for the Girgashite departed and is not mentioned in the Torah except in the verse \"וְנָשַׁל גּוֹיִם רַבִּים מִפָּנֶיךָ\" etc. (Deuteronomy 7:1), and therefore He said \"many.\" And likewise it is written (ibid. 20:17) \"כִּי הַחֲרֵם תַּחֲרִימֵם הַחִתִּי וְהָאֱמֹרִי הַכְּנַעֲנִי וְהַפְּרִזִּי הַחִוִּי וְהַיְבוּסִי,\" and He did not mention the Girgashite, to hint that he will not engage with them in battle and will depart from before them."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:07:23.960685193Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}